<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa, Namibia bourses to share information.</title>
<headline>S.Africa, Namibia bourses to share information.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Johannesburg Stock Exchange (JSE) said on Wednesday it had signed an information-sharing agreement with the Namibian Stock Exchange (NSE) as part of an initiative to build closer regional ties.  </p>
<p>Bourse regulators will exchange information to improve surveillance and investor protection.</p>
<p>Several companies with large investments in Namibia are listed on the JSE and dual-listed on the NSE, while many financial groups and market participants have operations in both countries.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
